{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"predict-output","title":"Predict the Output","group":"Interview Prep","order":64,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">The most common JavaScript interview format: read a snippet, say what it prints and <em>why</em>. Try each one before looking at the output.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-bar-up\"></i>1. Hoisting</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>var x = 1;\nfunction test() {\n  console.log(x);\n  var x = 2;\n  console.log(x);\n}\ntest();\nconsole.log(typeof hoisted, typeof expr);\nfunction hoisted() {}\nvar expr = function () {};</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>undefined\n2\nfunction undefined</code></pre></figure>\n<p>The local <code>var x</code> is hoisted to the top of <code>test</code> (as <code>undefined</code>) and shadows the global. <code>expr</code> is a <code>var</code> still holding <code>undefined</code> when <code>typeof</code> runs.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-repeat\"></i>2. Closures in loops</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const fns = [];\nfor (var i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) fns.push(() =&gt; i);\nconst fns2 = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) fns2.push(() =&gt; i);\nconsole.log(fns.map((f) =&gt; f()), fns2.map((f) =&gt; f()));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 3, 3, 3 ] [ 0, 1, 2 ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-pointer\"></i>3. this</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const obj = {\n  name: \"obj\",\n  regular() { return this.name; },\n  arrow: () =&gt; typeof this,\n  nested() {\n    const inner = () =&gt; this.name;     // arrow borrows nested()'s this\n    function plain() { return this; }  // plain call → undefined (strict)\n    return [inner(), plain()];\n  },\n};\nconst { regular } = obj;\nconsole.log(obj.regular(), obj.arrow(), obj.nested());\ntry { regular(); } catch (e) { console.log(e.constructor.name); }</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>obj undefined [ 'obj', undefined ]\nTypeError</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-refresh-dot\"></i>4. Event loop ordering</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(1);\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(2), 0);\nPromise.resolve().then(() =&gt; {\n  console.log(3);\n  setTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(4), 0);\n  Promise.resolve().then(() =&gt; console.log(5));\n});\n(async () =&gt; {\n  console.log(6);\n  await undefined;\n  console.log(7);\n})();\nconsole.log(8);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>1\n6\n8\n3\n7\n5\n2\n4</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Sync first (1, 6, 8). Then microtasks in queue order: the <code>then</code> (3, which queues 5 and timer 4), the <code>await</code> continuation (7), then 5. Finally macrotasks in order: 2, then 4.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-transform\"></i>5. Coercion</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(1 &lt; 2 &lt; 3, 3 &gt; 2 &gt; 1);\nconsole.log(\"5\" + 3, \"5\" - 3, \"5\" * \"2\", true + true);\nconsole.log([] + null + 1, [2] * [3], {} + []);\nconsole.log(0 || null || \"\" || undefined, 1 &amp;&amp; \"a\" &amp;&amp; 0);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true false\n53 2 10 2\nnull1 6 [object Object]\nundefined 0</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>3 &gt; 2 &gt; 1</code> → <code>true &gt; 1</code> → <code>1 &gt; 1</code> → <code>false</code>. <code>[] + null + 1</code> → <code>\"\" + \"null\"</code> → <code>\"null\" + 1</code>. <code>||</code> returns the last operand when all are falsy; <code>&amp;&amp;</code> returns the first falsy one.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-copy\"></i>6. References and copies</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>let a = { n: 1 };\nlet b = a;\na.n = 2;\na = { n: 3 };\nconsole.log(b.n);\n\nconst arr = [1, 2, 3];\nconst copy = arr;\ncopy.push(4);\nconst spread = [...arr];\nspread.push(5);\nconsole.log(arr.length, spread.length);\n\nfunction change(o) { o.value = \"changed\"; o = { value: \"replaced\" }; }\nconst item = { value: \"original\" };\nchange(item);\nconsole.log(item.value);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>2\n4 5\nchanged</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-circle-dashed-check\"></i>7. Promises</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const p = new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"A\");\n  resolve(\"B\");\n  reject(\"C\");\n  console.log(\"D\");\n});\np.then(console.log).catch(() =&gt; console.log(\"never\"));\nPromise.reject(new Error(\"E\"))\n  .then(() =&gt; console.log(\"skipped\"))\n  .catch((e) =&gt; e.message)\n  .then((m) =&gt; console.log(m + \"!\"))\n  .finally(() =&gt; console.log(\"F\"));\nconsole.log(\"G\");</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>A\nD\nG\nB\nE!\nF</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-puzzle\"></i>8. Mixed bag</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(typeof typeof 1, typeof [] === typeof null);\nconsole.log([...\"abc\"].map(parseInt));\nconsole.log(0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3, 0.5 + 0.25 == 0.75);\nconst x = { a: 1 }, y = { a: 1 };\nconsole.log(x == y, JSON.stringify(x) === JSON.stringify(y));\nconsole.log([1, 2, 3].indexOf(3) &gt; -1 ? \"found\" : \"missing\", [10, 1, 3].sort().join());\nfunction Foo() { return this; }\nconsole.log(new Foo() instanceof Foo, Foo());</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>string true\n[ NaN, NaN, NaN ]\nfalse true\nfalse true\nfound 1,10,3\ntrue undefined</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>parseInt(\"a\", 0)</code> → <code>NaN</code> (radix 0 means default 10, but <code>a</code> is not a digit), then radix 1 is invalid, and <code>\"c\"</code> isn't a base-2 digit. <code>0.5 + 0.25</code> is exact because both are powers of two.</p></div></section>"}